(LST2-13 — the *expression* form of {...} interpolation does not dispatch
 on a nested element's runtime tag; only the *variable* form does.
 Written as verdict lines rather than raw prints because the failing case
 renders a live heap address that changes every run — see Discrepancy 7.
 Also covers: LST2-12 (the variable form carries the full list rendering).
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox LST2-13.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   variable form: [1, [2, 3], "four"]
   expression form does not dispatch on the tag
   expression form is fine for a scalar element
)
a list called nested is [1, [2, 3], "four"].
print "variable form: {nested}".
a text called rendered is "{element 2 of nested}".
If rendered is equal to "[2, 3]" then, print "expression form dispatches on the tag".
Otherwise, print "expression form does not dispatch on the tag".
a text called plain is "{element 1 of nested}".
If plain is equal to "1" then, print "expression form is fine for a scalar element".
Otherwise, print "expression form wrong even for a scalar element".
